import MassGap.StrongCoupling -- the strong-coupling cluster expansion, on the REAL Wilson connected correlator. The expansion is an EXACT finite algebraic identity at every beta (boltz_eq_subset_sum, corrNum_eq_subset_sum) -- no radius, no remainder, no convergence -- and every pair of activated plaquette subsets whose union carries no touching chain from p0 to pd cancels under an explicit exchange across p0's own component (nonbridging_sum_eq_zero), so wilsonCorrConn is a sum over BRIDGING pairs alone over Z^2 (wilsonCorrConn_eq_bridging_sum). card_connSets_le then counts the touch-connected cores at each size by ((touchDeg bd + 1)^2)^m -- proved by covering a connected set with a walk built by repeated DETOUR, two steps per new plaquette, steps drawn from neighbours-plus-stay-put -- with Fintype.card Pq in neither statement nor proof; card_rooted_pairs_ge proves in Lean that dropping connectedness lets the volume back in, so the hypothesis is load-bearing. hard_core_ratio_le discharges the exponentially small Z^2 on beta >= 0 ALONE, with no Mayer expansion and no Kotecky-Preiss, because the constrained outside sum is itself a partition function (subset_sum_eq_subPart). coreResummation_holds proves the reindexing onto cores, pairTerm_abs_le bounds each term with a derived constant 8, and wilsonCorrConn_abs_le_coreConst_mul_rate_pow assembles them: neither coreConst nor coreRate carries the lattice extent. siteAtHyper_not_mem_ball is the lag-to-ball bridge, with the step constant DERIVED as 1 from bd's own boundary word and shown sharp (touch_advances_one); raw_lag_radius_refuted proves the raw-lag form FALSE on the periodic torus, so circLag is the only correct index. An abstract half-line decay predicate and its 14 dependents were RETIRED as unreachable, and the reason is a theorem rather than an opinion: no_sep_family_of_reachable proves such a predicate's separation family unsatisfiable once the plaquettes are reachable, and wilsonCorrConn_eq_zero_of_no_ball pr