import MassGap.Majorization  -- the deterministic form of the disorder-susceptibility sign, with no probability in it. PAPER 8.4's chi_v = -dH/dbeta >= 0 is the one input the interior route cannot measure; stated about the SPECTRUM rather than the coupling it becomes a monotonicity along the straight segment p(s) = (1-s)r + s q, and entropy_antitone proves the Shannon entropy non-increasing there under one scalar start condition, 0 <= sum_k (q_k - r_k) log r_k. The whole content is termwise: (q_k - r_k)(log p_k(s) - log r_k) = r_k x_k log(1 + s x_k) >= 0, so the derivative never exceeds its value at s = 0. The point of the file is that the start condition is not an extra assumption where it matters. concentration_at_dominant discharges it outright for a point-mass limit q = e_j at r's heaviest component, since the sum is then sum_k r_k log(r_j/r_k), a divergence; concentration_of_majorizes discharges it for ANY aligned q that majorizes r, by summation-by-parts into sum_m D_m (log r_{m-1} - log r_m) with both factors nonnegative. So entropy_antitone_at_dominant and entropy_antitone_of_majorizes are unconditional, which is the Schur-concavity of entropy in the one direction the argument uses. No axiom, no reflection positivity, no transfer matrix.
import MassGap.EvenAperture  -- THE GAP SIDE, AXIOM-FREE. existence_and_gap_of_substrate_even depends on axioms [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] and nothing else, and so does everything under it -- the measure side via WilsonModel.ymFamilyTension was already clean. The axiom entered at ONE def, Complete.readYMAt, which certifies the read with wilson_reflection_positive_at; wilsonCorrAt itself is clean, so the correlation was never the carrier, the certificate was. readEven certifies the same correlation with the PROVED wilson_reflection_positive_at_even instead, which needs an even extent of at least 4 and a nonnegative coupling. EvenAp bundles that aperture, exists_evenAp_of_eventually takes it from any eventual set (cofinal), and A2_even replays ym_A2's proof -- ym_A2 also reported the axiom, through ymModel's mu rather than through reflection positivity. THE HYPOTHESIS IS STRICTLY WEAKER and the implication is proved: substrate_even_of_substrate derives the new input from the old. THE COST, stated rather than papered over: LatticeYM.mu is total while the proof needs beta >= 0, so readEven is built at max beta 0; readEven_eq_readYMAt shows the two reads are the SAME OBJECT on the nonnegative half-line, and readEven_eq_at_zero shows that below it the model's column is the beta = 0 column relabelled, not a claim about the negative-coupling ensemble. That is exactly the domain where su3_kernel_nonneg_iff says the Wilson cross kernel is not positive-semidefinite. Non-vacuity: rp_at_extent_four is unconditional at any beta >= 0 and readEven_apFour_rho is rfl, so the axiom-free object at extent four is the constructed 4-D periodic SU(3) Gibbs correlation, not a stand-in.
