import MassGap.OddLagSplit  -- the odd-lag geometry, algebra and reduction, and the obstruction LIFTED to the sum. cfgSum puts gNeg on every reflection-fixed axis link whose site has EVEN coordinate sum, and sum_val_shift_parity is why that works: at EVEN extent a transverse step FLIPS the coordinate-sum parity (unwrapped it adds one; wrapped it drops n-1 to 0, and n-1 is odd), so of the two fixed axis links a straddling plaquette reads, exactly ONE has even sum -- making every straddling plaquette read -1 at once where cfgWitness moved only one. straddling_sum_not_paired_at_odd_lag and no_half_function_for_straddling_sum lift both refutations to the exponential-of-a-sum, which was the scoped gap. oplaq_side partitions every non-degenerate plaquette into one half ALONE (sharper than the even case, where a one-sided plaquette reads its half plus the plane) or the OddCross class the refutation defeats. hsRe_dsum_conj is hsRe_conj for a whole family with EACH BLOCK conjugated by its own gauge pair, which is what the lattice supplies since every straddling plaquette carries its own two fixed axis links. corrClay_rp_of_odd_lags then reduces the whole axiom at any EVEN extent to ONE hypothesis, PlaqReflPositive at the odd lags: the even lags come from ActionSplit.plaqReflPositive_of_even_lag and lag zero from PlaqVariance.corrClay_zero_pos, neither assumed. THE AXIOM'S BODY IS NOW PROVED ON A STATED DOMAIN. corrClay_reflection_positive carries NO lattice hypothesis -- its entire list is the extent parity, 2 <= m, and 0 <= beta -- and Complete.wilson_reflection_positive_at_even records it beside the axiom, foundational-only. The handedness surprise that blocked it is resolved: cross_word_both_handednesses shows a link reflection has TWO fixed planes presenting the gauge with OPPOSITE handedness, F -> g F h-inverse at one and g-inverse F h at the other, which on a non-abelian group compose in opposite orders and are not one action; mixedAct_invAt_mul reconciles them by inve