import MassGap.ContactFloor  -- THE CONTACT FLOOR, PROVED, so StrongArm's carried hypothesis is discharged and the strong arm is unconditional. wilsonCorrConn_self_ge_haar is the mechanism and it holds at every geometry and every SU(Nc): Var_beta(phi_p) >= exp(-2*beta*card(touchNbrs bd p)) * Var_0(phi_p), where the exponent counts the plaquettes SHARING A LINK with p and nothing else. The action splits as S_touch + S_rest because a plaquette that does not touch p reads none of p's links (rest_support, action_on_congr_of_support); e^{-beta*S_touch} lies in [e^{-2*beta*K}, 1] since each density is in [0,2]; the centred square and e^{-beta*S_rest} read DISJOINT link blocks so block_integral_factor factors them and the common integral of e^{-beta*S_rest} cancels against the partition function; and haar_centred_le discards the Gibbs mean, which carries both the coupling and the aperture, for the Haar mean, which carries neither. This is the step WilsonRead.expect_ge_haar_of_nonneg and wilsonSystem_partition_pos could not supply: their exponents are proportional to the PLAQUETTE COUNT and degrade as the lattice grows, while StrongCoupling.touchDeg_bd_le caps this one at 16*dim with no extent in it -- 64 at dim 4, so e^{-128*beta}. What remained was then an extent-uniform floor on the pure HAAR variance corrClay n 0 0, with no coupling left in it, and integral_hol_clay closes it: at extent n >= 2 the four links of the plaquette are distinct, so left-translating the LAST one (orientation false) sends the holonomy to hol*g, and averaging over g plus one Fubini swap identifies the law of the holonomy as Haar itself -- making corrClay n 0 0 the SAME number haarSecond - haarMean^2 at every n >= 2. Extent one is the one lattice where the four links are NOT distinct, so the pushforward has no starting point; it is handled as a single lattice, its variance a single number. The floor is therefore the min of two extent-free numbers times e^{-128*b}, and their POSITIVITY is PlaqVariance.corrClay_zero_pos -- non-constructive, and harmlessly so, because a universal constant is all the statement consumes; what had to be uniform in the aperture is the exponential, and touchDeg_bd_le makes it so. contact_relative_unconditional is contact_relative_on_strong_arm with nothing carried. THIS DOES NOT DISCHARGE THE SUBSTRATE HYPOTHESIS: that quantifies over every coupling and the cut b is still a cut, so [b, infinity) is untouched. The floor also DEGRADES as b grows, e^{-128*b}, which is the same behaviour GibbsPositive already flags -- a floor on each bounded coupling interval, not one number for the half-line. Foundational only.
import MassGap.NonnegArm  -- THE OBLIGATION, REDUCED TO ONE STATEMENT ON ONE INTERVAL. existence_and_gap_of_law_above_cut: there is a cut b > 0 -- the one contact_relative_unconditional produces, no numeral named -- such that LawAbove b alone gives the gap, non-triviality, SO(4) and the continuum measure. LawAbove b is the contact-relative quartic law for beta > b; the [0,b] arm is discharged INSIDE the theorem by lawBelow_holds, not assumed, and the two arms' constants merge at max C1 C2. THE NEGATIVE HALF IS DELETED, NOT ASSUMED AWAY: the reduction lands on d2Even, which is d2At at max beta 0, so the model is never evaluated below zero -- and by CharacterExpansion.su3_kernel_nonneg_iff the Wilson cross kernel is PSD iff 0 <= beta, so there was never a statement to be had there. Routing through the clamp also makes the composite AXIOM-FREE: the proof never mentions readYMAt, so wilson_reflection_positive_at never enters, and the nonnegativity the constant-merge needs comes from the PROVED wilson_reflection_positive_at_even. The continuum half is NOT weakened -- measure_is_ymFamilyTension checks by rfl that the measure side is the same object either way, so the substrate bound is consumed by the gap side alone. The one bridge that reports the axiom, substrate_at_nonneg_of_contact_relative_decay_nonneg, is labelled as such and is not in the chain.
