import MassGap.ApertureRoute  -- THE OBLIGATION IS CONFINEMENT AT ONE FINITE APERTURE. flagship_of_confinement_at_an_aperture: gap, non-triviality, SO(4) and the tight OS0-OS3 continuum limit from ConfinesAtAnAperture alone, which is exists a : EvenAp, forall beta, 3^(-1/4) < cosAvgEven a beta -- stated on the COSINE AVERAGE, not on the tension. That is not cosmetic: Moment.Read.tension is -Real.log of that average and Real.log is EVEN, so log(-1) = 0 and the tension form is satisfied by a read with NO DECAY AT ALL. unguarded_confinement_is_satisfiable_without_decay exhibits it at every aperture -- Substrate.antipodeRead, whose cosine average is exactly -1, and which is the very read the tree uses to show the 1/4 constant cannot be improved and that RP alone leaves the moment unbounded. The read that maximally violates the sufficient condition would have passed the unguarded necessary one. confines_iff_pos_and_tension_lt_floor proves the guarded form equivalent to (0 < cosine average) and (muEven < kappa_0YM), so nothing is strengthened by stating it this way. The substrate hypothesis was only ever consumed through Classical.choose to PICK one aperture -- fullModelEven's four fields take the aperture, not the bound, and the measure side takes nothing -- so the aperture quantifier is DROPPED, not satisfied, and no converse is claimed. That the weakening lost nothing is the theorem flagship_of_substrate_even_via_aperture. It was a definitional identity (Iff.rfl) before the guard; it is not one now, and the reason is benign -- the guarded hypothesis is a different existential, so Classical.choose need not pick the same extent. The conclusion's content is unchanged, only the witness. unguarded_of_confinesAtAnAperture machine-checks that the guard only RESTRICTS the hypothesis. THE EXTENT DOES NOT LOWER THE BAR: in ratio form the criterion is (2pi)^2 * substrateRatio / 2 < 1 - 3^(-1/4) with no N in it, because the aperture cancels EXACTLY (Complete.surplus_ge's hcancel, 