import MassGap.ReadLayer  -- THE ENTROPTICS READ LAYER, PORTED. The companion development at entroptics/research/lean/Entroptics was CITED by Certify.lean's header as [E, Lem 6.2] and never imported; it pins the same Lean and the same Mathlib rev, so it ported verbatim. tension_eq_log_sub proves the identity Moment.Read.tension's own docstring asserts and nothing proved: tension = log S(0) - log S(2pi/(N+1)), which is exactly the quantity the Weyl-certified band attenuation_weyl_certified propagates. So confines_at_an_aperture_of_certified reaches the flagship's hypothesis from TWO MEASURED NUMBERS AND ONE ERROR BAR rather than from an opaque tension. Also here: resolved_count_certified (the true resolved mode count enclosed by two read-side counts) and the entropy pair, which apply to Moment.Read.p with no adaptation since p is already a probability vector. WHAT IT DOES NOT GIVE, stated because the file is named for the thesis: propagator_recovers_charpoly does NOT produce Complete.WilsonSpectral -- it needs exact noise-free linear dynamics on a state vector and wilsonCorrAt is a Gibbs expectation with no A and no time index, its 'F modes' finiteness is a TYPE fact rather than a derived one, and its conclusion is a charpoly equality which gives neither real eigenvalues nor nonnegative weights nor the two-term shape. Reading-A is a MODELLING ASSUMPTION and Dynamics.lean does not justify it. The Entroptics layer bounds no absolute eigenvalue magnitude anywhere -- every statement is a ratio or a count -- so Aperture.lean's margin stays a hypothesis.
import MassGap.WeakArm  -- THE CONTACT BOUND AT EVERY LAG, and three proved no-gos on reaching the contact-relative quartic law from the coupling-free premises. corrClay_le_at_zero puts rho(d) <= rho(0) at EVERY lag, at even extent with m >= 3 and at EVERY real coupling, given only nonnegativity -- no floor on rho(0), nothing that degrades with the coupling, and invariant under rho -> t*rho. The even lags past the quarter are reached by the circle symmetry corrClay_neg, which turns corrClay_even_antitone's range 2c <= m into c <= m; the ODD lags, which no antitone result reaches because every right-hand lag log-convexity produces is even, are squeezed by corrClay_odd_le between two even neighbours already under rho(0) and the square root taken by nonnegativity -- m >= 3 is exactly the threshold that step needs, not slack. This does NOT contradict odd_scaling_admissible: that no-go forbids a LOWER bound on an odd lag and this is an upper one. wilsonCorrAt_le_at_zero discharges nonnegativity from wilson_reflection_positive_at_even, a theorem and not the named axiom, at the price of 0 <= beta; the conditional form is the one good at every real coupling and the two differ in scope. THE NO-GOS ARE THE OTHER HALF. no_contact_relative_from_shape exhibits, for every constant C and every cut m0, an extent and a profile satisfying MomentShape.Shape AND 0 < rho(0) AND 0 < sum rho -- Shape plus the two further facts available with NO premise depending on the coupling, corrClay_zero_pos (genuinely beta-free) and the second conjunct of the reflection-positivity theorem (every beta >= 0); the same two conjuncts are carried by no_strict_lag_bound_from_shape -- that violates rho(d) <= C*rho(0)/circLag(d)^4 past the cut. The witness is the CONSTANT profile, which is scale-free and carries no floor. no_strict_lag_bound_from_shape is the same witness against a constant factor: no t < 1 gives rho(d) <= t*rho(0) at any lag or extent, so the 1 in Part 1 is OPTIMAL for that premise set and